# apps/website/public/_headers — response headers for the public website (kwikserve.co.ke).
#
# `npm run build` copies public/ into out/, and the kwikserve-website Worker serves out/ as static assets with no
# script, so this file is the only way the site sends security headers. It follows decision D3 option 1 (PM stage 127;
# owner build basis 2026-10-04): the three lines the admin deployment already serves (apps/admin/public/_headers),
# plus a Permissions-Policy that turns off browser features this site never uses.
#
# Deliberately NOT here:
#   - X-Robots-Tag: the site, and above all the Terms, Privacy and account-deletion pages, must stay indexable (D8 (a)).
#   - Strict-Transport-Security: HSTS is a separate zone decision; includeSubDomains or preload would bind every
#     hostname under kwikserve.co.ke, including the mail names.
#   - Content-Security-Policy: a later, reviewed change (report-only first).
# The offline check is check-headers-file.mjs (package 79 checker) on the built out/ folder.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
